strategically the hills they're dying on. We talk a lot about these 90-10 issues where Trump will choose the 90 and they'll always choose the 10. There are Democrats where I look at them and I go, you know you're choosing the 10. You know this isn't a smart idea, so why are you doing it? And then hearing Stephen Miller say that, I thought,"], [0, "Now that would be a piece of the puzzle falling into place."], [0, "Well, I think it's always been like that since the early days of the mid-20th century where they discovered that they could hold dirt on people and bend them to their will until they're no longer useful. And outside of Congress, as a governor, Eric Swalwell wouldn't be very useful to the Democrats anymore. I mean, you're going to have a crazy Democrat as governor in California. That's just the way the state's rigged."], [0, "So Eric Swalwell stooping to that position or as he would see it rising to that position and maybe one day running for president again unsuccessfully isn't very useful to the Democrats. They don't need him anymore. He's just damaged goods and they wanted to do away with him."], [0, "Yeah, and oftentimes when you have people in politics, like, you get these stories. Who is that woman, Taylor? I always blank on her name. She had the thruple, like, combing somebody's hair. It's Katie something. It's not Katie Porter. It doesn't have to do with the potatoes. Um..."], [0, "It's that lady and I always blank on her name. Everyone's screaming it into their radios right now. I apologize. I can't think of her name. But you see things like that and you go, why does politics attract the biggest freakazoids known to man?"]], "participants": []}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversa