{"timestamp": 1778644567.421343, "duration_sec": 1.7544147968292236, "validator_hotkey": "5C8LULGoFybR7ybg4S8qQkaaowGXFFja4KmMoSqwhxuAsn33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Yeah, but my best experience is is with like, I got a chance to train against champions at their place, you know, when they're at their best. And it's not an ego thing. It's just like, I love to be able to test myself. And I mean, because I'm my biggest competition. And so that whole thing about just what the bow means to me is like, thank you for\u2014 making me better, right, by providing me an obstacle. And the higher the\u2014 you know, the better the person, the better I can become. 100%."], [1, "And so I loved it."], [0, "So I've, you know, for years I'm in there with Gokhan Saki and, you know, Maurice Smiths, and, you know, who\u2014 you know, you name it. I\u2014 there's\u2014 I've gotten\u2014 I consider myself one of the luckiest one of the greatest martial artists on the planet because I get to train with so many people. Sometimes at my house, and I've got all these former champions training. Rampage, when he was champion, I'd go to his place. And honestly, the things I brag about is when I get humbled. Because that's when I learn something. My philosophy is I love to be wrong because every time I'm wrong, I learn something. Something. Absolutely. And so, like, some of the best times for me is like, I know when I was, you know, Michael Bisping was getting ready for, to fight Georges St-Pierre, and we were in Thailand. I was like, yeah, you know, let's, let's like mix it up."], [1, "What were you doing in Thailand?"], [0, "Oh, we were doing a movie out there. Oh, wow. But he had to train. He was getting ready for the Georges St-Pierre fight. And so, you know, I was like, yeah, let's, let's do some rounds or whatever. And I got so winded the second round. I'm like, dude, just whoop my ass. I feel so like, like I'm embarrassed."], [1, "I should have been\u2014 was a cardio machine."], [0, "Yes, he was."], [1, "He was a cardio machine."], [0, "I didn't expect that because we were\u2014 we spent all day on a yacht the day before and he was drinking nonstop. I'm a non-drinker, right? I'm like, this guy's gonna, you know, yeah, I'm gonna probably take it easy on him today."], [1, "He is one of the toughest motherfuckers that ever fought in the sport."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["martial arts", "training", "sparring", "champions", "humility", "self improvement", "competition", "philosophy", "learning", "fitness", "cardio", "thailand", "film production", "yachts", "drinking", "sports entertainment", "discipline", "motivation"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
