Used Proforma Underwriting Guide - Tactica RES\u00ae\nAug 31, 2023 \u00b7 You may encounter a multifamily investment building with commercial (generally first-floor retail ). Today's blog post will give you a few ideas on underwriting the commercial space in a standard multifamily proforma model."], [2, "Financing Multi-Unit Projects: Challenges and Strategies\nIn multi\u2011unit markets, leasing speed and rental rates can shift rapidly. Conservative assumptions around absorption rates and lease\u2011up timelines improve resilience in changing conditions. Successfully navigating financing multi-unit projects demands expertise in cash flow management, lender expectations, and risk mitigation ."], [3, "Mixed-Use Development Projects: Maximizing ROI Through ...\nAug 8, 2025 \u00b7 Discover proven strategies for mixed-use development project planning that maximize ROI through strategic design, financing optimization, and market positioning. Learn expert frameworks for successful mixed-use projects ."]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["governance and intergovernmental relations committee", "city council", "board of transportation and infrastructure", "council resolution 26-0575", "council resolution 26-0576", "council resolution 26-0577", "council resolution 26-0578", "charter \u00a79.10.4(c)", "permanent panel of arbitrators", "permanent panel of mediators", "amanda sawyer", "paul kashmann", "kevin flynn", "stacie gilmore", "serena gonzales-gutierrez", "amanda sandoval", "jamie torres", "anne wallace", "mixed-use development", "tactica res"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778658932.7091193, "duration_sec": 2.100179433822632, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "99% Invisible is supported by Claude from Anthropic. There's a design decision happening right now that most people won't notice until it's too late. AI is about to get ads. You ask a question and the architecture of the response, what gets prioritized, what gets left out, starts being shaped by who paid for placement. Anthropic just committed to keeping Claude ad-free. No sponsored responses, no third-party influence shaping what you receive. Try Claude for free at Claude.ai/99invisible. 99invisible and see why problem solvers choose Claude as their thinking partner."], [1, "Time is valuable."], [0, "That's why Lowe's Blueprint Takeoffs turn blueprints into quotes faster. Bring us your plans and we'll generate itemized material lists to make quoting easier so you can get back to building. Plus, at the Lowe's Pro Desk, you get access to thousands of building materials not sold in store, and when your."], [1, "Order is ready, We'll deliver everything to the job site."], [0, "Improving is easy at Lowe's. This is 99% Invisible. I'm Roman Mars. The walk begins at the parking lot at the end of the road. The site isn't much to speak of, just a sprawling expanse of asphalt peppered with cars. Over a million people come here every year to embark on a kind of pilgrimage. They're here to cross the border."], [1, "We are getting ready to go to Mexico this morning. Yes, one more time. So we shall see what the rest of the day holds. There are hundreds of videos online documenting this experience. Watch as many as I did and they all start to meld together."], [0, "That's 99 PI producer Lashima Dawn."], [1, "Some people seem nervous in the videos. Others are more excited. Many will turn to their imagined audience behind the camera and speak in a reassuring tone. You see that American flag up there, y'all? This is one of the safest crossings there is. And it's not scary, I promise you. It is not scary. Everyone here is headed to the same town in Mexico. It's called Los Algodones, and it's a place where, for decades, Americans have roamed the streets. They come here in desperate search of something they need, something that's almost impossible to find where they live. They're looking for a dentist, one that they can afford."], [0, "Every day, thousands of people, mostly American, mostly white, and mostly retired, come to this town looking for relief from the turmoil in their mouths. Here, dental care costs up to 80% less than what it might cost in the US. Dental tourism to Los Algodones is so common that many call this place Molar City. Today, there are nearly 1,000 dentists in this 7,000-person town, and 98% of those in the patient's chair traveled here from outside Mexico. Lasha is going to take it from here."], [1, "Watch any one of these YouTube videos, and you'll see how a trip to Molar City is made easy for an American. For decades, this crossing didn't even require a passport. In one video, a retired couple arrives at Arizona's edge. They do a 360, displaying the massive lot where they've just parked. \"We love Mexico,\" they say emphatically, talking to the camera. The camera then pans to show the rust-colored border wall in front of them. That corrugated monstrosity. They marvel. Then a US Border Patrol vehicle starts driving past the screen, on guard, it seems, for anyone trying to cross in the opposite direction. To this, the camera woman speaks again, as if she's talking directly to Border Patrol. \"Get 'em, boys,\" she says. Then they begin their walk into Mexico. In Los Algodones, there are dense clusters of medical offices and a canopy of billboards above them. Vendors are set up on sidewalks where they sell handmade goods and kitschy souvenirs, like this one graphic tee that says, \"Keep calm, you're on the fun side of Trump's wall.\" And then there are the street promoters, people who are stationed at almost every street corner. Each of them competing for superlatives: the best deal, the quickest appointment, the most popular clinic in town. In Molar City, a street promoter is the first person a tourist will encounter."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["advertising", "artificial intelligence", "sponsored content", "claude", "anthropic", "design decisions", "construction services", "lowes", "blueprints", "border crossing", "mexico travel", "dental tourism", "healthcare costs", "dentistry", "retirees", "immigration policy", "medical marketing", "travel videos"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778659544.8564622, "duration_sec": 2.524825096130371, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "As a manager, you might believe that this only goes one way, that that kind of messaging that they are providing you is only increasing your uncertainty about what's going on."], [0, "But you've also received a decrease in another kind of uncertainty."], [0, "For example, before the meeting, you could pretty unequivocally say that you knew less about this person's state of mind than you do after."], [0, "This doesn't necessarily mean that you have an exact understanding of what's going on, but the signals that this person gave had a positive amount of information available for you to learn from."], [0, "So why is this all useful to talk about on this show?"], [0, "Why are we discussing this on Developer T?"], [0, "Certainly, if you have a CS degree, you may have had some kind of information theory class."], [0, "And it is definitely a foundational concept in computer science, but that's not necessarily why we're talking about it on this show, other than to kind of take advantage of the fact that many of you probably already know something about this theory to begin with."], [0, "Instead, because so much of what we do on the show is about decision-making, and that goes back to the idea of helping provide clarity, perspective, and purpose, all three of those things will help you enable decision-making in your careers."], [0, "Information theory is kind of the fundamental material that you will use to make decisions."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["management", "messaging", "uncertainty", "meetings", "state of mind", "signals", "information", "information theory", "computer science", "cs degree", "decision making", "career development", "communication", "psychology", "leadership", "problem solving", "learning", "workplace dynamics"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778659740.1315157, "duration_sec": 2.3915021419525146, "validator_hotkey": "5FZe9Mpo5dLXfhGZ4VjRnw6dmz9LVPp6nzqPyDfaS9BLKs33", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[2, "Agua Dulce was a very small town with lots of cantinas, and used to come people from Yuma to dance in the cantinas or drink."], [1, "This is Dr. Jesus Medina. He moved to town fresh out of med school in 1973, and he's been working here as a doctor ever since, although he seems to be perpetually on the brink of retirement."], [2, "I think one day I have to retire. And my sons tell me, \"When you gonna retire?\"."], [0, "Why?"], [2, "I'm too young to retire."], [1, "Dr. Medina first learned about Los Algodones from his brother-in-law, Dr. Bernardo Maga\u00f1a, who's often described as the godfather of Molar City."], [2, "He was the first dentist from this town, you know?"], [1, "Maga\u00f1a's now in his 80s. He is retired and didn't want to be interviewed. But Medina told me about how his brother-in-law Maga\u00f1a first had this vision to transform the town into a dental mecca. Back in the '60s, Maga\u00f1a and Medina were living together in a city about 25 miles from Algodones. Maga\u00f1a was a young dentist looking for a place to set up his private practice. At the time, he was working for someone who already had a few American patients. Patients who likely lived in the South and would cross into Mexico to take advantage of lower prices."], [2, "Gladstone started to tell about Algodones. He says, \"Why don't you move to Algodones? Because Algodones is 4 minutes from Yuma.\" He says, \"If you go there, you're going to have a lot more patients.\"."], [1, "At first, Maga\u00f1a was skeptical. He paid Los Algodones a visit, and it was a lot like he expected. A sleepy little place with a lot of mostly drunk people. But many of those drunk people were Americans. Its proximity to the border meant there was already a culture of coming and going. He saw the Americans spending their money at the bars and thought maybe they'd spend money on dentistry too. Maga\u00f1a knew he could offer them a price lower than what they could get in America."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Society & Culture"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["small town", "cantinas", "border town", "yuma", "los algodones", "mexico", "medical doctor", "dentistry", "dentist", "retirement", "private practice", "dental tourism", "cross border travel", "healthcare pricing", "american patients", "local economy", "entrepreneurship", "community transformation"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
