me."], [0, "Because your approach will be event-driven. Because in fact, the sidecar will ask your component first if you are interested into subscribing to any topic that is exchanged in the messaging, in the publish and subscribe building block."], [0, "And it will ask for the endpoint that the sidecar has to call to inform you that the new message or event has been received. So you will simplify a lot. This is really helpful from my experience and the perspective I have during these days working with customers."], [0, "Yeah, and something you said I really appreciate as well. And it's come up before you've mentioned development locally versus directly against cloud resources and assets. And I'm a huge fan as much as possible, and I push it pretty far if possible, to do development entirely locally."], [0, "Because when the internet goes down or GitHub goes down or whatever else goes down, especially if you need, oh, I can't get to SQS because my AWS cluster is this or that or my Kubernetes cluster is once again, you know, on the fritz. It's like, well, hold on. I can do everything locally."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["dapr", "microservices", "event driven architecture"