{"timestamp": 1778697597.6683776, "duration_sec": 1.8856782913208008, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "You probably have something you can do quick a minute. And if you fit in enough of those little hunks of tiny little tasks, you realize, oh, I actually got quite a bit done. That would have taken me a whole day. Like even with this office project is, I only have an hour after work today to work on something. Should I do it or not? And then at the end of the week, you say, well, I put in an hour every day. I actually got a lot done. That's a whole Saturday's worth of work, just doing it quick a minute."], [0, "Just quick minute. I've never heard of quick minute. I have heard of downtown job. Those are kind of different philosophies. I think the downtown job is a much longer process here. You're going to be taking extra time. So quick minute, downtown job. What if you did a downtown job quick minute? That'd be a pretty neat little innovation there. Yeah, well, you could still do a downtown job. It's just about..."], [0, "dicing up the downtown job into uh tasks that can be done quick a minute so if you've only got an hour 20 minutes here or there a downtown job by the way is scott's dad invented just doing a downtown job doing a great job and he revealed to me that he didn't invent it his dad is the one who always said it it was his three generations"], [0, "Yeah, that's Ernie Talinsky right there with the downtown job. Ernie, have you told Landon about downtown job? No, I should have. Landon said, oh, my God. Kids really do be saying the darndest things. Landon said to us at the dinner table, I felt like this