ve fund and a stable and equitable funding plan to offset ongoing deterioration, resulting in sufficient funds when those anticipated major common area expenditures actually ..."], [2, "Environment, Land Use & Natural Resources Advisory\nJul 7, 2025 \u00b7 Two newly enacted California Environmental Quality Act ( CEQA ) reform laws (AB 130 and SB 131) would significantly impact California\u2019s infill housing sector. Our Environment, Land Use & Natural Resources Group unpacks what developers and other stakeholders need to know about the changes."], [3, "Governor Newsom Signs 2025 CEQA Reform Bills (AB 130 and SB ...\nNov 18, 2025 \u00b7 AB 130 (a budget trailer bill focused on housing) introduces a new statutory CEQA exemption for qualifying \u201cinfill\u201d housing projects. In essence, many urban housing developments that meet specified criteria can now be approved without undergoing CEQA , substantially shortening the approval timeline ."]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["city of oakland", "oakland city hall", "oakland city council public safety committee", "charlene wang", "rowena brown", "carroll fife", "ken houston", "california environmental quality act (ceqa)", "ab 130", "