0 or something like that. And Matt was like, what? It was like, that's just the way we talked. Like we didn't even think about it. Like it wasn't even. Oh, that's so funny. So good. Oh, all right. It's got to take a little bit of work."], [0, "Yeah. Val Kilmer resurrected by AI to star in as deep as the grave. So I think, I think if I understood this correctly, he had already committed to the film. Yeah. And then he passed away. And so the film worked with his estate to get permission and worked with all of the, all of the acting agencies and all that, whatever they are. Yeah. Guilds, I think to get permission and about, we're going to have an AI Val Kilmer."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Technology"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["artificial intelligence", "data centers", "energy prices", "public relations", "elon musk", "tesla", "self driving cars", "netflix", "acquisitions", "film industry", "ai filmmaking", "actor likeness", "entertainment business", "celebrity startups", "machine learning", "media regulation", "digital resurrection", "labor unions"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
